speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, the second order deals with the membership of Standing Committees, and again I think you find a disposition to receive the following order by unanimous consent and to have it passed without debate:
That the following changes be made in the membership of the Standing
Committees:
Aboriginal Affairs and Northern Development, Pietz for Nickerson; Consumer and Corporate Affairs, Nickerson for Lawrence;
External Affairs and International Trade, Johnston (Saint-Henri-West-mount) for Gray (Windsor West);
Finance and Economic Affairs, Nicholson (Trinity) for Johnston (Saint-Henri-Westmount);
Human Rights, King for Pietz;
Multiculturalism, Jacques for Lesick; and Transport, Dantzer for Belsher.
